# f1 = groupBy, f2 = shownBy, f3 = named, f4 = shown
# The scan said "the answer is read as a key" only of a call that is the first argument of a method of Map or Set. A helper handed in as a callback, compiled alone, whose answer another function reads
# as `groups[key]`, gave a rope, and each access under it turned the rope into a name (57% of the peer's 16-group-summary.mjs). The key of an access under a key says the same as the argument of Map.get.
# RUN: walk f3:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f3:Body
# CHECK: Strcat {{*}} [isLikelyKey]
# CHECK: Strcat {{*}} [isLikelyKey]
# CHECK: frequency=Rare
# CHECK: Add {{*}} form=Generic
# RUN(SHOWN): walk f4:Body mechanisms=all
